# SCRIPT: txn_Commit
# FOLDER: 00_APP
# ROLE: close the pseudo-transaction — the ONE place a commit is allowed to happen
# CALLED BY: every routine that opened with txn_Begin, on the success path
# CALLS: commitRecord (utilities) for the validation-error message contract
# INPUTS: none
# GLOBALS IN: $$TXN_ACTIVE, $$TXN_PARENT_TABLE, $$TXN_PARENT_ID, $$TXN_LABEL
# RETURNS: { ok } | { ok:false, error, errorCode }
# GLOBALS OUT: clears $$TXN_*
# SIDE EFFECTS: commits the parent record AND every related record written since txn_Begin
#
# 🚨 THIS IS THE ONLY `Commit Records` ALLOWED BETWEEN txn_Begin AND HERE.
#   Every other commit in a write routine is a bug. Not a style problem — a bug. A stray
#   commit ends the transaction early and makes the preceding writes permanent, so a later
#   failure rolls back only the remainder. The routine still reports success and the ledger
#   is silently half-written.
#   ⛔ 60_PAYMENTS__Auto_Apply_Waterfall currently commits TWICE PER APPLIED ROW inside its
#      loop. That is the single most important thing to strip when it is rewritten.
#
# WHY IT FAILS LOUDLY AND NEVER SWALLOWS:
#   A wrapper that eats an error to keep a routine moving is worse than no wrapper, because
#   the caller believes the write landed. On any commit error this returns ok:false with the
#   FileMaker error code and leaves the record UNCOMMITTED so the caller can roll back.
#   It does not decide for the caller and it does not retry.
#
# VALIDATION ERRORS ARE NOT TRANSACTION ERRORS:
#   507 (validate by calc), 506 (required), 504 (unique) mean the DATA is wrong, not that
#   the transaction broke. Those route through the shared `commitRecord` helper so the
#   user-facing wording is single-sourced from MSG_ValueListErrors instead of being
#   re-invented here. Get(LastError) returns a code, never the field's own message —
#   which is exactly why that helper exists.
#
# 🥇 STATE: GOLDEN — designed, not yet built.
#
# CHANGELOG:
#   - 2026-07-29 designed alongside txn_Begin / txn_Rollback. Michael, DL Q3: rollback and
#     error catching throughout, not per-routine improvisation.

# --- GUARD: refuse to commit a transaction nobody opened ---
Set Error Capture [ On ]

If [ $$TXN_ACTIVE <> 1 ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "txn_Commit called with no open transaction" ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- RETURN TO THE PARENT so the commit lands on the anchor record, not wherever the
#     routine happened to leave the found set ---
Go to Layout [ $$TXN_PARENT_TABLE ]

# --- THE COMMIT ---
Commit Records/Requests [ With dialog: Off ]
Set Variable [ $err ; Value: Get ( LastError ) ]

If [ $err ]
	# leave it UNCOMMITTED and hand the decision back. Do not revert here — the caller
	# owns the rollback so it can log first.
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "commit failed in txn " & $$TXN_LABEL ; JSONString ] ; [ "errorCode" ; $err ; JSONNumber ] ) ]
End If

# --- CLEAR STATE only after a clean commit ---
Set Variable [ $$TXN_ACTIVE ; Value: "" ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_ID ; Value: "" ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_PARENT_TABLE ; Value: "" ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_PARENT_ID ; Value: "" ]
Set Variable [ $$TXN_LABEL ; Value: "" ]

Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; True ; JSONBoolean ] ) ]
